     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** The usual adult dose of amlodipine is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the maximum. 50 mg is five times the maximum, which is in overdose range. It could cause severe low blood pressure and shock. It may be a typo (for example, 5 mg) or a mix-up with another drug.\n\n**2. Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician, so you don't have prescribing authority for this patient, whatever your role at the hospital. Even with a corrected dose, the order needs to come from the patient's treating physician, nurse practitioner, or PA, who can check it against the patient's full history.\n\n**Next steps:** Contact the attending physician or covering prescriber on the medicine service. If you were passing along an order you received, please check the intended drug and dose with whoever wrote it. Once a prescriber confirms the order, I can help them enter it."
      }
     ],
