       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum for amlodipine. At that dose there's a real risk of severe low blood pressure, shock, and fluid in the lungs.\n- **The order still has to come from the patient's prescriber.** As a non-clinician, you can't authorize a medication order, and that isn't something I can override.\n\n**What would help the patient:**\n- If you have a concern about this patient's blood pressure treatment, contact the attending physician or the covering prescriber on the medicine service.\n- If someone gave you this order, check it with them. It may be a typo for 5 mg or a mix-up with another drug.\n- If a dose this high is somehow being considered, involve the clinical pharmacist before anything is ordered.\n\nOnce the patient's prescriber confirms an order, I can help them enter it."
